// W4e surface fold-in — shell redirections, pipelines, and list operators
// (parse-only fixture).
//
// GRADUATION: the shell DSL's redirection class, pipelines, and control / list
// separators are exercised as real molded forms (wyrd-83wx). The redirection
// operators (`>`, `>>`, `<`, `<&`, `>&`, `<>`) were already molded; W4e makes
// the file descriptor (`2>`, `2>&1`) real — a digit run abutting a redirection
// now molds as `file_descriptor` (grammar.js `file_descriptor`) rather than a
// stray shell word, so `redirection` captures `fd op target` properly. The
// pipeline `|` / `|&` is a binary infix; `&&` / `||` and `;` / `&` are the
// control and list separators. The SEMANTICS (wiring these to the host
// Exec/Fs/Proc effects) graduate under the wyrd-83wx gandr-shell wiring
// follow-up — a shell block today still lowers only flat simple commands, so
// these forms parse but do not yet run. Parse-only; never lowered.
//
// NOTE: commands are kept SHORT (few juxtaposed atoms per block). Shell command
// juxtaposition is O(atoms^2) in the melder today (each juxtaposed atom triggers
// a Degrout that walks the slope) — a pre-existing hazard flagged for a follow-up
// (making the `command` rule absorb arguments as form-continuations). Short
// blocks keep this fixture well inside the batch p99 budget.

// Output, append, and input redirections.
#!{ echo hi > out; }
#!{ echo more >> out; }
#!{ cat < in; }

// A redirection file descriptor: stderr to a file, and stderr merged to stdout.
#!{ make 2> err; }
#!{ make 2>&1; }

// Pipelines: plain `|` and the stderr-merging `|&`.
#!{ cat data | sort; }
#!{ make |& tee log; }

// Logical control (`&&` / `||`) and the list separators (`;` / `&`).
#!{ probe && report; }
#!{ probe || abort; }
#!{ warm; run & }
